  "body": "Residue from the 2026-07-17 harness session (commit ec7f066), filed so the watch items survive the conversation.\n\n1. **RUNLOG enforcement gate (patterns.yml) has not fired on a real run yet.**\nThe next scheduled patterns run (Sunday 05:17 UTC, 2026-07-19) is its first live fire. Verify: a legit run (including a no-op that logs) passes the \"Enforce RUNLOG rule\" step, i.e. the grep path `KnowledgeBase/BoardGames/patterns/RUNLOG.md` matches what the pass actually commits. If the gate false-positives on a legit run, fix the gate, not the rule.\n\n2. **Decision made, revisit if incidents recur: the new Stop hook (okf-guard.mjs stop) ships warn-only by default.**\n`KB_STRICT_STOP=1` makes it block (with a 3-strike cycle breaker) but no workflow sets it. Rationale: warn-only cannot wedge a scheduled pass; strict mode is opt-in per workflow if silent-leftover incidents (dirty tree / unpushed commits at turn end) show up in practice.\n\nClose when the first live patterns run is verified and the strict-mode call is either affirmed or flipped.\n",
